(4438106, 636604, 75958, '<td valign="top">well... this is unexpected, going to be hearing about this for a bit.congratulations!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-30 00:06:42.</i></td>', 'well... this is unexpected, going to be hearing about this for a bit.congratulations!', '2008-01-30 00:05:56.000000', '2008-01-30 00:06:42.000000', 0),
(4438114, 636984, 61961, '<td valign="top">Congrats on making the top 25, this was one of my challenge favorites.</td>', 'Congrats on making the top 25, this was one of my challenge favorites.', '2008-01-30 00:07:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4438143, 634697, 67237, '<td valign="top">Too bad it was the same idea used by a few others. I am sure that has afected the score.<br/>About possible improvements:<br/>*better if one of the leather seats was not intersecting one of the poles.<br/>*a bit shallower dof to isolate the main subject a bit more from the bg.<br/>*duotone works fine but it eliminates the use of color to isolate main subject from bg, so some S/H adjustment could have been made to avoid the merging.<br/>*a little tighter crop on top and left would have helped to get more detail at 640px dpc.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-01-30 20:15:19.</i></td>', 'Too bad it was the same idea used by a few others. I am sure that has afected the score.About possible improvements:*better if one of the leather seats was not intersecting one of the poles.*a bit shallower dof to isolate the main subject a bit more from the bg.*duotone works fine but it eliminates the use of color to isolate main subject from bg, so some S/H adjustment could have been made to avoid the merging.*a little tighter crop on top and left would have helped to get more detail at 640px dpc.', '2008-01-30 00:15:02.000000', '2008-01-30 20:15:19.000000', 0),
(4438152, 636604, 30982, '<td valign="top">Congrats, Leo!</td>', 'Congrats, Leo!', '2008-01-30 00:17:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4438155, 636292, 88575, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by socalsteve:</b></div><hr/><i> How did you do this? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I reversed the image to a negative, then played with hue, saturation, and colors.  I guess it was a little creepy for most people.  ;)</td>', 'Originally posted by socalsteve: How did you do this?   I reversed the image to a negative, then played with hue, saturation, and colors.  I guess it was a little creepy for most people.  ;)', '2008-01-30 00:17:39.000000', NULL, 0),
