(4440250, 635513, 5885, '<td valign="top">I like it... fun photo. I''ve got a few issues (keep in mind I didn''t vote):<br/> <br/>1) the branch from the tree, looks like it''s trying to pet his head or something. <br/>2) DoF is a bit too deep, adding distractions in the background and a shallower DoF could have fixed the tree issue.<br/>3) I''m sure the blown sky hurt you a bit. DPC loves either blue skies or skies with a lot of features. A relector or flash on the subject could have kept exposure correct on the subject while giving you a darker sky and darker background, making the subject more prominent.<br/>4) I like the motion in the hand, but shutter spped increase could have made focus on the subject a tad sharper.<br/> <br/>Anyway, I hope I haven''t been overly critical, but DPC, as you know, is a picky crowd. If you want high scores, you have to cater to that finickiness. If you want to have fun, well, you kinda have to not worry about scores.<br/></td>', 'I like it... fun photo. I''ve got a few issues (keep in mind I didn''t vote): 1) the branch from the tree, looks like it''s trying to pet his head or something. 2) DoF is a bit too deep, adding distractions in the background and a shallower DoF could have fixed the tree issue.3) I''m sure the blown sky hurt you a bit. DPC loves either blue skies or skies with a lot of features. A relector or flash on the subject could have kept exposure correct on the subject while giving you a darker sky and darker background, making the subject more prominent.4) I like the motion in the hand, but shutter spped increase could have made focus on the subject a tad sharper. Anyway, I hope I haven''t been overly critical, but DPC, as you know, is a picky crowd. If you want high scores, you have to cater to that finickiness. If you want to have fun, well, you kinda have to not worry about scores.', '2008-01-30 14:00:54.000000', NULL, 0),
